in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @uuid
in @epistemologic/property/content_addressed
in @epistemologic/property/laws/monoidal

# @uuid/spectral — the graph-navigatable spectral identifier.
#
# The first sub-prism under @uuid (the universal 128-bit identifier
# discipline at shards/uuid.mirror). Specializes the universal carrier
# into the navigable spectral form: a 128-bit identifier whose leading
# bits carry a route signal (graph-navigable) and trailing bits carry
# an identity signal (content hash). The TOP layer of Alex's
# 2026-06-06 three-layer recognition (see shards/glass.mirror's
# header and docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md §1B).
#
# === The hierarchical factoring (2026-06-06) ===
#
# The previous tick landed `@mirror/store/spectral_uuid` as an opaque
# `ref` parallel to `@mirror/store/oid`. Alex pushed back: "if
# spectral_uuid is an opaque type how can the mirror fate inference
# (the mycelial conductivity bit) use it to route?" The opacity hid
# exactly the thing Fate's mycelial routing needs to read. Alex then
# sharpened the factoring further: @uuid becomes a root prism (the
# universal 128-bit identifier); @uuid/spectral is one variant under
# it. The substrate gains hierarchical UUID vocabulary; the spectral
# variant gains a navigable structure Fate can route through.
#
# === The 128-bit layout, golden-ratio split ===
#
# Per prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs and
# [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] §3:
#
#   128 bits, golden-ratio split (≈1/φ²):
#     48 bits ACTIVE  — quantized SpectralCoordinate<5>; leading;
#                       graph-navigable. Carries the local Laplacian
#                       neighbourhood structure within a shard's
#                       splinter OID graph. Fate's mycelial routing
#                       reads through this portion.
#     80 bits DARK    — BLAKE3-truncated content hash; trailing;
#                       identity. The settled splinter set's
#                       content-address prefix.
#
# Big-endian on the active portion: byte-wise sort over the leading
# bits IS lexicographic sort over the navigable coordinate. Range
# scans on the 48-bit space compose with byte-wise sort. The standard
# UUID hyphenated form (8-4-4-4-12) layers over the byte layout
# directly; hyphens land at positions 4, 6, 8, 10. The byte layout
# IS enforced by the realization layer (prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs);
# the substrate altitude declares the semantic structure.
#
# === Monoid homomorphism w.r.t. shard merge ===
#
# Per docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §3:
#
#   uuid_spectral(merge(a, b)) = combine(uuid_spectral(a), uuid_spectral(b))
#
# Both halves compose homomorphically:
#   - dark 80 bits compose via the Merkle tree's content-address rule;
#   - active 48 bits compose via SpectralCoordinate's eigenvalue
#     addition law (to first order; weighted by content size).
#
# `empty` is the semilattice's bottom — λ₀ = 0 in spectral space,
# BLAKE3-of-empty in content space. The four monoid axioms (identity,
# associativity, commutativity, idempotency) hold by structural
# consequence of content-addressing + sorted-children, per
# reality-shard-as-crdt.md §1. The `requires monoidal(uuid_spectral)`
# declaration at the bottom is the substrate's compile-time witness.
#
# === Semantic types over byte primitives (Touch 1 / α) ===
#
# Per the 2026-06-06 Touch 1 decision: substrate declares route_signal
# and identity_signal as semantic types of meaning, not byte counts.
# Fate routes through `route_signal`; content-verification reads
# `identity_signal`. The 48/80 byte split is enforced at the Rust
# realization layer; substrate doesn't need bit-width primitives. The
# separation prevents accidental conflation in downstream code (Fate's
# mycelial routing has a typed handle for the navigable portion;
# verification has a typed handle for the identity portion).
#
# === The deferred arithmetic ===
#
# Per reality-shard-as-crdt.md §11 OQ1, the quantized 48-bit
# arithmetic for `combine`'s active portion is still being pinned —
# it lands when SpectralCoordinate<5>'s eigenvalue composition rules
# quantize cleanly. The `combine` action below is declared with a `\`
# obligation block; the signature is well-defined (the monoid laws
# constrain it), the body is deferred to the same tick that pins the
# arithmetic.
#
# Spec: docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §§2, 3, 11.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: uuid.mirror (the root prism this glass is under),
#                 glass.mirror (shard.id IS uuid_spectral),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (shard_ref = uuid_spectral),
#                 mirror/mosaic.mirror (the algebra A whose D acts on
#                                       the uuid_spectral-indexed H).
# Reference: [[reference-void-document]] (λ₀ = 0 IS empty.active).
# Realisation: prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs (the carrier; this shard
#              names what the carrier IS at the substrate altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/uuid/spectral.mirror`
# declares `@uuid/spectral` and only that.

# Sub-prism under @uuid. The glass keyword (per @glass) marks this
# as a sub-prism scoped to the @uuid parent.
glass @uuid/spectral {
  focus uuid_spectral
  project uuid_spectral
  split uuid_spectral
  shift uuid_spectral
  settle uuid_spectral
}

# === Semantic substrate types ===
#
# route_signal — the navigable handle. Fate's mycelial routing reads
# through this. Carries the local Laplacian neighbourhood position
# within a shard's splinter OID graph; range scans on byte-sort
# correspond to navigation on the spectral coordinate. The byte-width
# (48 bits) is a realization-layer fact, not a substrate-altitude fact.
type route_signal = ref

# identity_signal — the content-identity handle. Content-verification
# reads through this. Carries a BLAKE3-truncated content hash; opaque
# to routing. Two uuid_spectrals with byte-equal identity_signal are
# composed from byte-equal splinter sets. The byte-width (80 bits) is
# a realization-layer fact.
type identity_signal = ref

# === uuid_spectral — the record ===
#
# The two semantic signals composed into one carrier. Equality at the
# uuid level (per @uuid.equals) is byte-equality of the resulting
# 128-bit reference; equality at the variant level decomposes into
# byte-equality of (active, dark).
#
# The record form is what makes route_signal and identity_signal
# substrate-visible. The realization layer (prism/core/src/
# spectral_uuid.rs) composes them into the big-endian 16-byte
# carrier; the substrate altitude carries the typed pair.
type uuid_spectral = {
  active: route_signal,
  dark:   identity_signal,
}

# === empty — the bottom of the semilattice ===
#
# Per docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §2: the canonical empty-
# shard address. λ₀ = 0 on the active 48 bits (the void axis per
# [[reference-void-document]]); BLAKE3 of empty input on the dark 80
# bits (the well-known constant `af1349b9f5f9a1a6a040`). Stable
# across all BLAKE3 implementations; byte-stable in the carrier.
#
# `fixed` per boot/std/mirror/glass/ast/shape/fixed.mirror: a fully
# settled crystal, content-addressed on declaration, no holes, no
# inference. The OID of this binding IS `empty`'s identity at the
# substrate altitude. The realization layer (prism/core/src/
# spectral_uuid.rs::EMPTY) is the byte-stable carrier; this
# declaration names the substrate-altitude fixed point.
fixed empty = uuid_spectral

# === active — project the navigable signal ===
#
# Project the route_signal out of a uuid_spectral. The quantized
# SpectralCoordinate<5> Fate routes through. Range scans on the
# active portion compose with byte-wise sort (the big-endian layout
# is what makes this work). Body deferred to the realization layer.
active(u: uuid_spectral) -> route_signal { \ }

# === dark — project the identity signal ===
#
# Project the identity_signal out of a uuid_spectral. The
# BLAKE3-truncated content hash. Two uuid_spectrals with identical
# dark portions are composed from byte-equal splinter sets. Body
# deferred to the realization layer.
dark(u: uuid_spectral) -> identity_signal { \ }

# === combine — the monoid homomorphism ===
#
# Per docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §3:
#
#   uuid_spectral(merge(a, b)) = combine(uuid_spectral(a),
#                                        uuid_spectral(b))
#
# The active 48 bits compose via SpectralCoordinate's eigenvalue
# addition law (to first order; the spectral position of a union of
# content is the sum of the constituent positions weighted by content
# size). The dark 80 bits compose via the Merkle tree's existing
# content-address rule.
#
# Monoid laws (encoded by `requires monoidal(uuid_spectral)` below):
#
#   identity:        combine(empty, a) == a == combine(a, empty)
#   associativity:   combine(combine(a, b), c)
#                       == combine(a, combine(b, c))
#   commutativity:   combine(a, b) == combine(b, a)   (per §1: from
#                                                    sorted children)
#   idempotency:     combine(a, a) == a               (per §1: from
#                                                    content-address)
#
# The signature is well-defined; the body is deferred per the spec's
# §11 OQ1 — the quantized 48-bit arithmetic lands when
# SpectralCoordinate<5>'s eigenvalue composition rules quantize
# cleanly. Until then, the realization layer's `from_parts` re-derives
# the identifier from fresh inputs and `empty` carries the
# bottom-element semantics.
combine(a: uuid_spectral, b: uuid_spectral) -> uuid_spectral { \ }

# === Properties: the math made load-bearing ===
#
# content_addressed(uuid_spectral)
#   Identity IS the content hash. Foundational; inherited from @uuid
#   (the root prism), restated here at the variant altitude for the
#   record shape. Two uuid_spectrals with byte-equal carriers ARE the
#   same uuid_spectral.
#
# monoidal(uuid_spectral)
#   combine + empty form a monoid. Identity, associativity per
#   @epistemologic/property/laws/monoidal. Commutativity + idempotency
#   follow from the semilattice structure (reality-shard-as-crdt.md
#   §1) — captured in the docstring; the substrate-altitude property
#   declaration uses the existing `monoidal` carrier (the parked
#   `identity_for` / `commutative` / `idempotent` extensions per
#   reality-shard-as-crdt.md §10 tick 3 are not yet declared, and per
#   the discipline land when their first consumer surfaces).
#
# A `navigable(uuid_spectral)` property would name the substrate-level
# fact that Fate's mycelial routing reads through `active`. The
# property does not yet exist in @epistemologic/property; declaring it
# is a separate substrate tick (surfaced for Alex). Until then, the
# fact lives in the route_signal type's semantics (Fate consumes
# route_signal by type; the substrate has the handle).
requires content_addressed(uuid_spectral)
requires monoidal(uuid_spectral)

out @uuid/spectral
out uuid_spectral
out route_signal
out identity_signal
out empty
out active
out dark
out combine
